      "text": "A and B are both stored the same way, row after row.\n\nEach thread needs a row of A and a column of B.\nSo the A tile keeps the block's rows and slides right, one tile per phase.\nThe B tile keeps the block's columns and slides down, one tile per phase.\n\nEvery thread loads the value at its own position in the tile.\nLaid over the tile, not over its own spot in C.\n\nRule of thumb: A slides along the rows, B slides down the columns,\nand each thread always takes the same position in the tile.",
      "fontSize": 16,
